{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfZjvyLvurdNmEuHns2zd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe consolidation is structurally clean and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- **Single check replaces three, coherently.** `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` collapses the email/telephone/household checks into one function that compares whole `identityKey`s, and it correctly switches its input from `@Val OwnerFieldsDto` to `@Val Owner` because it must run after `BuildOwner`/`AssignOwnerHousehold` have produced the entity and resolved `householdId`. The YAML reordering (check now after `assignHousehold`) matches that dependency, and the step docs were updated to reflect it.\n\n- **Exception/handler surface shrinks without duplication.** The three near-identical handlers become one; renaming the Email handler to `DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler` and deleting the redundant Telephone/Household ones is the right move rather than leaving three copies of the same ProblemDetail body.\n\n- **Shared helpers relocated to their sole remaining user.** `sameHousehold`/`normalize` moved from the deleted `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique` into `AssignOwnerHousehold`, which is now their only consumer — the logic followed its user rather than being orphaned or left in a dead class. `AssignOwnerHousehold` stays cohesive (all household-assignment concerns), not a catch-all.\n\n- **`getIdentityKey()` sits naturally on `Owner`.** This matches the existing `getPreferredContactMethod()` precedent of derived, response-only getters on the entity, so exposing it there for both the response DTO and the check is consistent with the codebase's own convention, and `keyPart` keeps null-safety encapsulated as a private static.\n\n- **No dangling references.** The javadoc `@link`s in `NormalizeOwnerAddress`, `NormalizeOwnerEmail`, and `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` were all updated to drop the now-deleted check classes, and the OpenAPI schema documents the new `identityKey` field consistently.\n\n(Note: whether `getIdentityKey()` composing raw stored fields — rather than re-normalizing existing owners the way the old checks did — matches all stored data is a behavioral/correctness question, which is out of scope for this structural review.)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21369,"cache_read_input_tokens":11894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21369},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb4c6115-9081-49c9-92f2-f940b2f2b745","uuid":"e80d0a1a-0c3e-4807-a6a7-7faf5cc0265f","timestamp":"2026-09-30T13:58:32.927Z","request_id":"req_011CfZjvxy74Z72VLdyjr1mY"}
